This is the summary of the problem in my mind. The kicker is having to
remove the nonbroken armor, which is pretty much untenable in an
extended melee, which again, is essentially guaranteed at some point
in the game.

Hence the suggestion that blessed confused scrolls pick damaged armor
to repair. This way, you "only" have to take the time to  (a) spend a
turn getting the scroll out of your bag and (b) spending a turn each
to get confused, read the confused scroll, and unconfuse yourself.  As
well as the effort prepare the scrolls ahead of time and carry them.

Even having blessed confused scrolls *favor* damaged armor by
something like the chance unicorn horns have of fixing sickness would
be something.

